			},
			"date": "2026-11-21T16:25:35.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> My impression: It comes down to what someone thinks a website should be.</p><p>If a website is dynamic (and not a collection of documents) then, to me, it is an app: I want it to be offline first and sync with a data server. That way, it works even if the internet is flaky.</p><p>However, many people want their websites to work without JavaScript and their pages rendered as quickly as possible—even on slow devices. Then you need server-side rendering (right?).</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
